     6	  comment CONSTANTS stages 1 and 2 have none. A line 3: k, the integer value of z in the equation z = k of stage 3;
     7	  comment P01a. Unknowns x, y, z. Stage 1: x = y. Stage 2: y = z. Stage 3: z = k. ALGOL 60 has no unknowns, so each unknown is a Boolean that says whether it has a value and an integer that holds it, and each equation is held as posed until a place is known, when it gives the other place its value or is tested. The only value any stage gives is an integer, so the integer holds every value an unknown can take here;
     8	  integer n, cap, m, i, code, k, c3, xv, yv, zv, held, pass;
     9	  Boolean xk, yk, zk, r1, r2, r3, changed, inconsistent;
    10	
    11	  procedure equation(ak, av, bk, bv, r);
