  6	  comment CONSTANTS a line 1: L e1 ... eL, the length and then the elements of the known sequence a of conc(a, s, t). A line 2: L e1 ... eL, the length and then the elements of the sequence of s = b. Elements are integers, an atom being its integer code;
  7	  comment P01b. Unknowns s and t, sequences. Stage 1: conc(a, s, t). Stage 2: s = b. A sequence is a cell index into the arrays hd and tl, 0 being the empty sequence, and a cell c being the sequence hd[c] followed by the sequence tl[c]. The cells are kept in arrays of a fixed size, cells, since a stage's sequence is read only when its stage is posed. Each unknown is a Boolean that says whether it has a value and the sequence it holds. Each relation is held as posed until enough of its places are known;
  8	  integer cells;
  9	  cells := 1000;
 10	  begin
 11	  integer n, cap, m, i, code, k, len, top, a1, b2, sv, tv, held, pass, conc1, conc2;
 12	  Boolean sk, tk, r1, r2, changed, inconsistent;
 13	  integer array hd, tl[1:cells];
 14	
 15	  integer procedure cons(h, t);
 16	    value h, t; integer h, t;
 17	  comment a new cell, the sequence h followed by the sequence t;
 18	  begin top := top + 1; hd[top] := h; tl[top] := t; cons := top end cons;
 19	
 20	  integer procedure readseq(len);
 21	    value len; integer len;
 22	  comment a sequence of len elements, read from the input in order;
 23	  begin
 24	    integer j, e, first, last, c;
 25	    first := last := 0;
